{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvacPpJotddhJ8r4xiPr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gate's cost on clean answers splits into 5 format failures and 18 right→wrong flips (against 9 wrong→right). The flips look like drift: GSM samples wander into alternative interpretations at 12–13k tokens where the brake-only version finished correctly in about 5k. There are also a few copy slips, e.g. a correct 1/13·[[4,−6],[−6,9]] in the thinking boxed as a garbled matrix, and remainders 1,3,3,1 read off as 133. That is the price of weakening line-start copying everywhere. The rescued loops outweigh it (+14.8 vs brake only), but it limits how much more gating can help. Since remaining gains will be small, I want any further anti-loop step to target a clear copying pathway. One candidate I haven't tested is L23H6. It is a last-layer \"duplicate-token\" head that put 0.60 of its attention on the previous cycle's identical line-start token. In the last layer, that token's residual mainly encodes what was predicted there last time, so a copying OV circuit would reinforce the loop directly. I'll screen all full-attention heads' OV circuits for same-token copying. If L23H6 is a strong positive copier, it is a principled addition to the gate; if it is neutral or suppressive, I'll drop the idea.\n\n```python\n# OV same-token copy score for all FA heads (mean z of own-token logit over 1500 common tokens); is L23H6 a positive copier?\nrng=np.random.default_rng(0); cand=rng.choice(np.arange(1000,60000),1500,replace=False)\ndef ov_self(L,h,ids):\n    Wv=load(f'model.language_model.layers.{L}.self_attn.v_proj.weight'); Wo=load(f'model.language_model.layers.{L}.self_attn.o_proj.weight')\n    lnw=load(f'model.language_model.layers.{L}.input_layernorm.weight'); kv=h//4\n    x=E[ids]; x=x/x.pow(2).mean(-1,keepdim=True).sqrt()*(1+lnw)\n    lg=((x@Wv[kv*256:(kv+1)*256].T)@Wo[:,h*256:(h+1)*256].T)@E.T\n    z=(lg-lg.mean(1,keepdim=True))/lg.std(1,keepdim=True); idx=torch.arange(len(ids))\n    return float(z[idx,torch.tensor(ids)].mean())\novs={(L,h):ov_self(L,h,cand.tolist()) for L in [3,7,11,15,19,23] for h in range(8)}\nsrt=sorted(ovs.items(), key=lambda x:-x[1])\nprint('top copiers:', [(f\"L{L}H{h}\",round(v,1)) for (L,h),v in srt[:10]])\nprint('gated:', [(f\"L{L}H{h}\",round(ovs[(L,h)],1)) for (L,h) in sorted(gated)], '| dup heads:', [(f\"L{L}H{h}\",round(ovs[(L,h)],1)) for (L,h) in [(23,6),(7,6),(7,7),(3,7),(11,3),(15,5)]])\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4907,"cache_read_input_tokens":92678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4907},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e01c29c3-4f30-44c6-bee0-870b4ff8f3f8","uuid":"524689af-2c4c-4965-9959-3942a8d401ca","timestamp":"2026-11-11T05:23:08.653Z","request_id":"req_011CgvacPWhc9uQgE7ZV4WdZ"}
